# 低频词汇 List03
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List03核心词汇

{{backbone}}{/ˈbækbəʊn/}{脊柱；支柱}{Small businesses are the backbone of the economy.}}
{{badge}}{/bædʒ/}{徽章；标记}{Employees must wear their ID badges at all times.}}
{{bail}}{/beɪl/}{保释；保释金}{The suspect was released on bail pending trial.}}
{{bait}}{/beɪt/}{诱饵；引诱}{The advertisement was designed as bait to attract customers.}}
{{ballot}}{/ˈbælət/}{选票；投票}{Voters cast their ballots in the national election.}}
{{ban}}{/bæn/}{禁止；禁令}{The government imposed a ban on smoking in public places.}}
{{bankruptcy}}{/ˈbæŋkrʌptsɪ/}{破产}{The company filed for bankruptcy after years of losses.}}
{{barbecue}}{/ˈbɑːbɪkjuː/}{烧烤；烤架}{We had a barbecue in the backyard on Saturday.}}
{{baron}}{/ˈbærən/}{男爵；巨头}{He was a media baron who owned several newspapers.}}
{{barren}}{/ˈbærən/}{贫瘠的；不育的}{The barren landscape showed no signs of life.}}
{{basement}}{/ˈbeɪsmənt/}{地下室}{The basement was converted into a home office.}}
{{batch}}{/bætʃ/}{一批；一组}{The factory produced a new batch of products.}}
{{beam}}{/biːm/}{光束；梁；微笑}{A beam of sunlight entered the room through the window.}}
{{behalf}}{/bɪˈhɑːf/}{代表；为了}{The lawyer spoke on behalf of the victims.}}
{{benevolent}}{/bɪˈnevələnt/}{仁慈的；慈善的}{The benevolent donor funded the construction of a school.}}
{{bestow}}{/bɪˈstəʊ/}{授予；赐予}{The university bestowed an honorary degree upon her.}}
{{betrayal}}{/bɪˈtreɪəl/}{背叛；出卖}{The betrayal by his partner left him devastated.}}
{{beverage}}{/ˈbevərɪdʒ/}{饮料}{The café serves a variety of hot and cold beverages.}}
{{bizarre}}{/bɪˈzɑːr/}{奇异的；怪异的}{The plot of the movie was bizarre but entertaining.}}
{{blade}}{/bleɪd/}{刀片；叶片}{The grass blades glistened with morning dew.}}
{{blast}}{/blɑːst/}{爆炸；一阵}{A blast of cold air hit them as they opened the door.}}
{{blaze}}{/bleɪz/}{火焰；熊熊燃烧}{The blaze destroyed several buildings in the area.}}
{{blend}}{/blend/}{混合；融合}{The coffee is a blend of beans from different regions.}}
{{bless}}{/bles/}{保佑；祝福}{She felt blessed to have such a supportive family.}}
{{bliss}}{/blɪs/}{极乐；幸福}{Ignorance is bliss, as the saying goes.}}
{{block}}{/blɒk/}{街区；阻塞}{A fallen tree blocked the road after the storm.}}
{{blunt}}{/blʌnt/}{钝的；直言不讳的}{His blunt criticism hurt her feelings.}}
{{blur}}{/blɜːr/}{模糊；使模糊}{The line between work and home life has blurred.}}
{{boast}}{/bəʊst/}{夸耀；自夸}{He boasted about his achievements at the meeting.}}
{{bold}}{/bəʊld/}{大胆的；醒目的}{She made a bold decision to start her own business.}}
